  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Boundaries that hold",
      "items": [
        "The policy page and the connect handover need an Access JWT for the lollo's own application (CF_LOLLO_AUD); Lettuce's JWT is refused",
        "Every tool checks the stored level, allowed recipients, self-events and shared mailboxes when it runs, so calling /mcp directly gains nothing",
        "The token is sealed with OUTLOOK_SECRET, which lives only in this service's environment, on a volume nothing else mounts",
        "/mcp answers only Host lollo-outlook with no Origin; the tunnel routes only /outlook/ to it",
        "Microsoft is called directly (trust_env off), and lollo-outlook is in NO_PROXY, so pipelock never sees the token or the mail"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Not a boundary",
      "items": [
        "BFF and app-server share one network namespace; agents run as root in the app-server and can call /mcp",
        "The allowed recipients guard the account's identity, not what an agent reads within its level",
        "The FOCI redemption is unsupported by Microsoft: a tenant can refuse it, and the page then says so"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not shown",
      "items": [
        "Other lollo pages on the same host (vault, Gmail triggers, News Radar, the code editor) and Lettuce's opt-in services",
        "Outlook on the web itself, where the bookmarklet reads the cached sign-in",
        "lolloctl on the host: generates OUTLOOK_SECRET, holds the service to check_outlook (hardened, default network only, only outlook-data), registers outlook in Settings -> MCP (lolloctl mcp)"
      ]
    }
  ]
